Jym wrote:
> 
> I usually have no big trouble letting my large 
> cat/dog  kill the first unicorn I met and I'm even glad to let it eat 
> the corpse to  get hand on the horn...

If I happen to have a pet at the moment when I see a unicorn I often
even lose the pet due to that contact. Other cases are that my pet or
I myself kill the unicorn, but it's far from guaranteed or easy (as I
said depending on role played and other circumstances), IME.

> At that time, I usually have not identified lots of potion (except  
> price-id) and #dip the horn in all of them. In almost every game I end 
> up  naming several potion "100$ - danger" because I don't know more 
> after  dipping the horn (and don't need to know more until I happen to 
> get full  ID from a scroll).
> And I always find swimming boring because it takes lots of time to 
> remove  and drop everything, go swim, find out that I was too lucky and 
> nothing is  blanked, and repeat. If I can grab enough harmful potions to 
> have enough  water just with the horn, I'm quite happy.

You can swim, or you can dip. Dipping into water costs two turns for
each stack of potions, dip testing with the unicorn costs as well two
turns if you first check with an unimportant item for polymorph. Going
to swim can dilute many potions and many scrolls in a few turns. I don't
think that the turns would be the problem, but undressing or dipping in
fountains can have some bad side effects; and I agree that a unihorn dip
is far safer. Diluting stacks of potions is faster with fountains/pools.

> Well, I guess your mileage may vary, of course, but I find the 
> horn/potion  interaction really useful at the time I met unicorns.

No, I agree that it is useful. I am just not guaranteed that I will get
the unicorn horn and there are other means to achieve the same (or with
even better outcome) than what the unicorn horn will do.

Don't get me wrong; a unicorn horn is part of my base equipment as soon
as I can get it. It's like the swiss army knife, capable of many things,
but you won't use it to cut down a tree, there are more effective items.

